---
// Work section — extracted from legacy index.html on 2026-05-20
---
<!-- ═══════════ CASE STUDIES ═══════════ -->
<section class="block" id="work">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">02 · Selected Work</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Flagship <em>engagements.</em></h2>
      <p class="section-sub">
        Seven projects showing the patterns I keep coming back to: headless commerce, regulated systems, ERP bridges, identity infrastructure, and high-traffic experience platforms. Each one names the business outcome first, then how it was built.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cases">

      <!-- CASE 01 · RUST-OLEUM -->
      <article class="case reveal">
        <div class="case__visual">
          <div class="case__visual-meta">
            <div class="left"><strong>DWG · A–01</strong><span>React Hybrid / Page Builder</span></div>
            <div class="right"><strong>Fortune 500</strong><br>D2C · Coatings</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__shot">
            <img src="/assets/projects/rustoleum.png" alt="Rust-Oleum storefront — homepage screenshot" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="case__body">
          <div class="case__client"><strong>Rust-Oleum</strong> · Home</div>
          <h3 class="case__title">A storefront that <em>scales without breaking operations.</em></h3>
          <div class="case__role">Role · <b>Principal Architect</b></div>

          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Outcome</div>
            <div class="case__row-v case__row-v--outcome">Marketing-owned page composition without breaking checkout, tax, or ERP integrity.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Challenge</div>
            <div class="case__row-v muted">A Fortune-500 catalog was stranded inside platform constraints. Marketing wanted richer product experiences; ops wanted to keep the BigCommerce checkout, tax, and ERP integrations they already depended on.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Solution</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">Designed a React hybrid page-builder layer for BigCommerce — a custom storefront embedded into the Page Builder workflow so marketing could compose experiences without losing checkout, tax, or back-of-house stability.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Tech</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">
              <div class="chips">
                <span class="chip is-key">React</span>
                <span class="chip is-key">BigCommerce</span>
                <span class="chip">Page Builder</span>
                <span class="chip">TypeScript</span>
                <span class="chip">Tailwind CSS</span>
                <span class="chip">Stencil</span>
                <span class="chip">Node.js</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- CASE 02 · PACKRUSH -->
      <article class="case case--alt reveal">
        <div class="case__visual">
          <div class="case__visual-meta">
            <div class="left"><strong>DWG · A–02</strong><span>Fulfillment Storefront</span></div>
            <div class="right"><strong>D2C · Logistics</strong><br>Ship-from-Store</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__shot">
            <img src="/assets/projects/packrush.png" alt="Packrush — fulfillment storefront screenshot" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="case__body">
          <div class="case__client"><strong>Packrush</strong> · packrush.com</div>
          <h3 class="case__title">A storefront wired into <em>real fulfillment.</em></h3>
          <div class="case__role">Role · <b>Lead Engineer</b></div>

          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Outcome</div>
            <div class="case__row-v case__row-v--outcome">Customers see honest delivery math at the cart; ops never reconciles shipping surprises.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Challenge</div>
            <div class="case__row-v muted">A logistics-forward D2C operation needed a storefront tightly coupled to fulfillment — quoting, packing rules, and shipping math had to live next to the catalog, not behind it.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Solution</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">Built a modern headless storefront with <em>real-time shipping</em>, packaging logic, and order orchestration baked into the buying flow.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Tech</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">
              <div class="chips">
                <span class="chip is-key">Next.js</span>
                <span class="chip is-key">TypeScript</span>
                <span class="chip">Node.js</span>
                <span class="chip">Stripe</span>
                <span class="chip">Shipping APIs</span>
                <span class="chip">Tailwind CSS</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- CASE 03 · NUUN -->
      <article class="case reveal">
        <div class="case__visual">
          <div class="case__visual-meta">
            <div class="left"><strong>DWG · A–03</strong><span>ERP ↔ Headless Bridge</span></div>
            <div class="right"><strong>10-Year Partnership</strong><br>Startup → Global</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__shot">
            <img src="/assets/projects/nuun.png" alt="Nuun — hydration brand storefront screenshot" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="case__body">
          <div class="case__client"><strong>Nuun</strong> · Hydration</div>
          <h3 class="case__title">Startup to <em>global, in stages.</em></h3>
          <div class="case__role">Role · <b>Technical Partner · 10 yrs</b></div>

          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Outcome</div>
            <div class="case__row-v case__row-v--outcome">Kept inventory truth online through three commerce platform transitions.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Challenge</div>
            <div class="case__row-v muted">A category-defining brand growing past every commerce platform they tried. Each scale-jump risked breaking the ERP, inventory truth, and operational workflows the warehouse and finance teams actually trusted.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Solution</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">Owned the <em>custom middleware</em> architecture between NetSuite and a headless Shopify storefront on Next.js — guiding the brand through three platform generations without ever taking inventory truth offline.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Tech</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">
              <div class="chips">
                <span class="chip is-key">NetSuite</span>
                <span class="chip is-key">Shopify Headless</span>
                <span class="chip is-key">Next.js</span>
                <span class="chip">Celigo</span>
                <span class="chip">Node.js</span>
                <span class="chip">TypeScript</span>
                <span class="chip">Liquid</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- CASE 04 · DC iLOTTERY -->
      <article class="case case--alt reveal">
        <div class="case__visual">
          <div class="case__visual-meta">
            <div class="left"><strong>DWG · A–04</strong><span>Geofenced iGaming</span></div>
            <div class="right"><strong>Government</strong><br>Federal-Grade Compliance</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__shot">
            <img src="/assets/projects/dcilottery.png" alt="DC iLottery — geofenced iGaming platform screenshot" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="case__body">
          <div class="case__client"><strong>DC iLottery</strong> · Intralot</div>
          <h3 class="case__title">A platform built for <em>auditability.</em></h3>
          <div class="case__role">Role · <b>Lead Architect</b></div>

          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Outcome</div>
            <div class="case__row-v case__row-v--outcome">A government-regulated platform that stays defensible to regulators while staying usable on the front end.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Challenge</div>
            <div class="case__row-v muted">Build a high-security iGaming platform — native and web — for the District of Columbia's lottery. Every flow had to be defensible to a federal-grade regulator, every event replayable, every wallet enforceable.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Solution</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">Architected a hard-perimeter system: <em>geofencing</em> with layered GPS+IP signals, responsible-gaming workflows wired into every entry point, and an auditable event log for post-hoc compliance reconstruction.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Tech</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">
              <div class="chips">
                <span class="chip is-key">React Native</span>
                <span class="chip is-key">Node.js</span>
                <span class="chip">TypeScript</span>
                <span class="chip">AWS</span>
                <span class="chip">PostgreSQL</span>
                <span class="chip">Geofencing SDKs</span>
                <span class="chip">Crypto/KYC</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- CASE 05 · AGEVERIFY -->
      <article class="case reveal">
        <div class="case__visual">
          <div class="case__visual-meta">
            <div class="left"><strong>DWG · A–05</strong><span>Identity SDK</span></div>
            <div class="right"><strong>Proprietary</strong><br>Privacy-First IDV</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__shot">
            <img src="/assets/projects/ageverify.png" alt="AgeVerify — privacy-first IDV SDK screenshot" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="case__body">
          <div class="case__client"><strong>AgeVerify</strong> · SDK</div>
          <h3 class="case__title">Identity, <em>without surveillance.</em></h3>
          <div class="case__role">Role · <b>Founder / Engineer</b></div>

          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Outcome</div>
            <div class="case__row-v case__row-v--outcome">Verifiable age gates with no PII at rest — compliance without a privacy liability.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Challenge</div>
            <div class="case__row-v muted">Regulated industries need verifiable age gates — but most IDV vendors turn private documents into someone else's database. A proper boundary needed to be engineered, not configured.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Solution</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">Built a proprietary IDV <em>SDK / API</em> on Azure serverless infrastructure with a strict cryptographic privacy boundary — verification at the edge, no PII at rest, immutable proof for compliance without bulk data hoarding.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Tech</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">
              <div class="chips">
                <span class="chip is-key">Azure Functions</span>
                <span class="chip is-key">Cosmos DB</span>
                <span class="chip is-key">TypeScript</span>
                <span class="chip">Node.js</span>
                <span class="chip">Crypto / Hashing</span>
                <span class="chip">React SDK</span>
                <span class="chip">REST / Webhooks</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- CASE 06 · LAN SU CHINESE GARDEN -->
      <article class="case case--alt reveal">
        <div class="case__visual">
          <div class="case__visual-meta">
            <div class="left"><strong>DWG · A–06</strong><span>Cultural · Nonprofit</span></div>
            <div class="right"><strong>Public-Facing</strong><br>Events · Ticketing · CMS</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__shot">
            <img src="/assets/projects/lansu.png" alt="Lan Su Chinese Garden — website screenshot" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="case__body">
          <div class="case__client"><strong>Lan Su Chinese Garden</strong> · lansugarden.org</div>
          <h3 class="case__title">A garden, <em>online and alive.</em></h3>
          <div class="case__role">Role · <b>Lead Developer</b></div>

          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Outcome</div>
            <div class="case__row-v case__row-v--outcome">A small in-house team publishes events, tickets, and shop content without engineering involvement.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Challenge</div>
            <div class="case__row-v muted">A landmark cultural nonprofit needed a public-facing site that could carry rich storytelling, a constantly shifting events calendar, ticketing, membership, and the Garden Shop — all editable by a small in-house team.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Solution</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">Designed and built a <em>content-rich CMS-driven site</em> with editorial flexibility for events, exhibits, and the teahouse — pairing a fluid layout system with structured content for low-friction publishing.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Tech</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">
              <div class="chips">
                <span class="chip is-key">CMS</span>
                <span class="chip is-key">PHP</span>
                <span class="chip">JavaScript</span>
                <span class="chip">Custom Theme</span>
                <span class="chip">Ticketing Integration</span>
                <span class="chip">Responsive UI</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- CASE 07 · TIMBERLINE LODGE -->
      <article class="case reveal">
        <div class="case__visual">
          <div class="case__visual-meta">
            <div class="left"><strong>DWG · A–07</strong><span>Hospitality · Resort</span></div>
            <div class="right"><strong>Iconic Property</strong><br>Booking · Conditions · Trails</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__shot">
            <img src="/assets/projects/timberline.png" alt="Timberline Lodge — Mt. Hood resort website screenshot" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="case__body">
          <div class="case__client"><strong>Timberline Lodge</strong> · timberlinelodge.com</div>
          <h3 class="case__title">A mountain <em>at full resolution.</em></h3>
          <div class="case__role">Role · <b>Senior Engineer</b></div>

          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Outcome</div>
            <div class="case__row-v case__row-v--outcome">One year-round digital home that holds conditions, lodging, and editorial without feeling like separate sites.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Challenge</div>
            <div class="case__row-v muted">An iconic Mt. Hood resort needed a year-round digital home — ski conditions, lift status, mountain biking, dining, lodging, and a deep historical brand — without ever feeling like a stack of disconnected mini-sites.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Solution</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">Architected a high-traffic <em>all-season experience platform</em> tying together real-time conditions feeds, lodging, activity content, and editorial — engineered to scale through peak-season surges and surface the right information for whichever season the visitor showed up in.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="case__row">
            <div class="case__row-k">Tech</div>
            <div class="case__row-v">
              <div class="chips">
                <span class="chip is-key">ProcessWire</span>
                <span class="chip is-key">PHP</span>
                <span class="chip">JavaScript</span>
                <span class="chip">Conditions Feeds</span>
                <span class="chip">CDN / Caching</span>
                <span class="chip">Custom CMS</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
